KOBO — PERSONAL BUDGET TRACKER

Overview
--------
Kobo is a local-first budget tracker for recording income and expenses in their
original currencies. It brings transactions, monthly totals, category spending
and an optional spending target into one view, without requiring a bank
connection or account.

It solves a familiar problem: money can move across currencies and across notes,
receipts and bank apps, making it difficult to tell what came in, where it went
and how spending compares with a plan. Kobo keeps each calendar month separate.
A surplus, deficit or target does not carry into the next month, and monthly net
is not a running bank balance.

What you can do
---------------
- Record transactions in NGN, USD, EUR, GBP, JPY, CNY, CAD, AUD, CHF, INR or ZAR.
- Choose each transaction's original amount, currency, category and date.
- Choose a monthly budget currency and set an optional spending target in it.
- Change View in to see totals, chart and transactions in another currency,
  without changing the target's currency or percentage used.
- See the original amount and each conversion's rate, date and provenance.
- Use a manual rate or derive an effective rate from a bank-charged amount.
- If the exact-date rate is unavailable, enter one or explicitly accept an
  earlier published rate; affected totals remain labelled incomplete otherwise.
- Receive in-app warnings at 75% and 100% of a monthly spending target.
- Export a monthly CSV report, or download and restore a full JSON backup.
- Use labelled sample data in an otherwise empty month.

Using the tracker
-----------------
1. Pick a month. NGN is the default budget currency for a new month. Use Change
   beside the budget currency to choose another currency for that month.
2. Set an optional target. It is measured in the budget currency, uses expenses
   only and does not change the month's net.
3. Choose Add transaction, select Income or Expense, and enter the original
   amount, currency, date and category. A description is optional.
4. Choose View in to display the month's totals and chart in another currency.
   The transaction date determines the historical rate, not today's rate.
5. Use Edit rate or Resolve rate on an entry to enter an effective bank rate,
   retry an exact-date reference rate or review an earlier published rate.
6. Use Backup to download the complete budget. The CSV button downloads only
   the selected month's transaction report and is not a restore file.

Amounts must be positive. JPY uses whole yen; the other supported currencies
accept up to two decimal places. Enter amounts without commas. A transaction or
target is limited to 999,999,999 whole units plus any allowed fractional units.
Saving a transaction in a different month switches the view to that month.

Each destination currency uses its own direct rate from the original currency.
A manual rate applies only to its transaction and currency pair. For example, a
manual USD-to-NGN bank rate is used for an NGN budget, but a separate USD-to-EUR
rate is used for an EUR view. The target and its progress always stay in the
monthly budget currency. Reference rates can differ from a bank's actual charge.

Data and privacy
----------------
The app stores transactions, targets, currencies and saved rate data in this
browser's localStorage. They are not encrypted, synced or backed up automatically.
Clearing site data, switching browsers or changing the site's origin can make
records unavailable. Current Kobo tabs coordinate one editable tab per origin;
other tabs are read-only until the writer closes. Editing requires HTTPS (or
localhost) and Web Locks. Close older app tabs before upgrading, as they may
not respect the lock. If a conflict occurs, download a backup before reloading.

Historical rate lookups go online. Rate providers receive the requested date and
currency pair or base, plus normal network information such as your IP address.
The app does not send transaction amounts, descriptions or categories in those
requests. Internet access is needed for automatic rates, but manual rates work
offline. Rates can be unavailable even when connected.

Backup files contain every month, transaction, target, currency and saved rate;
they are not encrypted. Store them privately. Restoring a valid backup replaces
the entire current budget after confirmation; it does not merge records. CSVs
contain only the selected month's transactions and cannot be restored.

If a storage warning appears, do not assume changes are saved. The app avoids
silently overwriting unreadable data. Keep the tab open and download a backup of
what is visible; unreadable records cannot be included in that backup.

Getting started
---------------
Install a currently patched Node.js 24 LTS and npm, then run from the project directory:

    npm ci
    npm run dev

Open the URL printed by Vite. Use npm test for domain and storage tests and
npm run build to create the static production build. See read.md for browser
tests, implementation details, rate sources and limitations. See DEPLOYMENT.md
for private production setup and the required access-control checks.
